# Copy to box/vyre.env (or /srv/vyre/vyre.env). The vyre service reads it if present.
# Never commit the real file.

# A Cloudflare API token scoped to the vyre.run zone, with DNS edit permission. vyred uses it
# to publish <you>.vyre.run and answer the Let's Encrypt DNS challenge. Needed until the
# hosted name directory exists.
# CLOUDFLARE_VYRE_TOKEN=

# Optional. A Tailscale auth key, read by the tailscale service (it takes it from the shell
# environment or /srv/vyre/.env, not from this file). Leave unset for interactive login:
# the onboarding page shows the login link.
# TS_AUTHKEY=

# Read from the shell environment or /srv/vyre/.env (not this file), for the `computers` profile:
# the group that owns /var/run/docker.sock on the host, so the docker-api proxy can use it
# without running as root. install-box.sh writes it from `stat -c %g /var/run/docker.sock`.
# DOCKER_GID=999
# What a computer's create may ask for; the proxy refuses any other. Keep in step with vyred's
# computers.* config. Defaults shown.
# VYRE_COMPUTERS_NETWORK=vyre-computers
# VYRE_COMPUTERS_IMAGE=vyre/computer:0.1
# VYRE_COMPUTERS_LABEL_PREFIX=run.vyre.computers
# VYRE_COMPUTERS_CAP_ADD=

# Read from the shell environment or /srv/vyre/.env (not this file: the vyre service reads all of
# this file into its environment, where Claude sessions would see the key), for
# box/compose.egress.yml only. An ephemeral, pre-authorized auth key tagged tag:vyre-egress, and
# the Mac to use as the exit node (its tailnet name or 100.x address). Then turn it on in vyred:
#   vyre call --tty computers.egress.set '{"enabled":true,"sites":["bank.example.com"]}'
# VYRE_EGRESS_AUTHKEY=
# VYRE_EGRESS_EXIT_NODE=alex-mac

# A note on updates: an update that runs as root (the automatic one from Settings, or `sudo vyre update`) does not read this file or .env as
# configuration. It passes on only CLOUDFLARE_*, VYRE_SETUP_CODE and VYRE_EGRESS_* from here, and DOCKER_GID, TS_AUTHKEY, VYRE_DRIVE_ACCESS and
# VYRE_TS_HOSTNAME from .env. VYRE_COMPUTERS_IMAGE, _NETWORK, _LABEL_PREFIX and _CAP_ADD are NOT passed on (the defaults apply, and no extra
# capability is ever added by an update run as root); the update names every setting it ignored. Set them for your own `docker compose up`.
